From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Thomson <git@mnt.dev>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 19:42:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [search] Online place search backed by Google

Adds a toggle in the search bar that sends queries to the Places API (New)
instead of the offline index: places:autocomplete for predictions, then
places/{placeId} for the coordinates and details of the one the user picks.

Autocomplete carries no coordinates, so a prediction is emitted as a
Result::Type::LatLon centred on the query origin and delivered with
hasPosition == false. Selection therefore goes through GetPlaceDetails()
rather than the result's own centre, and predictions are not turned into map
marks. Details reach the place page through the ordinary InjectMetadata path,
with opening hours converted to OSM opening_hours syntax, so no new
place-page section is needed for them.

Shares the "GoogleApiKey" setting with the Google router; without a key
nothing is requested.
